name iso-639-2
# The ISO 639-2 list as a table of five fields parted by |, without a header row. The file names none of its fields,
# and no documentation of them is kept with it, so no field is given a name: each row says its first field and each of
# its other fields side by side, in the row's own order, [first, other]. The numbers below only say where a field
# stands in the row; they are not recorded.
match ISO-639-2_utf-8.txt
# The file does not name who publishes it; the same list in loc/iso639-2.rdf is the Library of Congress's.
witness Library of Congress

tier row by \n
names 1 2 3 4 5
tier field by |

thing row 1
content 1 2 3 4 5
pair row 2 3 4 5
